title: 'Consequence: switching back gives the original a new viewnode ID where the clone stood.'
pid: 691253d1-1e7f-4cf2-89af-aa4e6e872152
body: |2-
  Switching to the user's re-points each substituted occurrence in
  place, so its viewnode ID, and the cursor on it, survive. Switching
  back takes the path an override's removal takes ('stop_substituting'):
  the original is reinstated beside the clone, which, no longer
  warranted, vanishes; so the cursor on the clone moves to the nearest
  headline. Where a third author's override stood (A for M, say), the
  occurrence is re-pointed and keeps its ID both ways.
